{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider 64 sent 0xa5 but UART data trap got 0xff vs want 0xa5, i.e. RX stayed idle. Root cause in excerpt is `if (reg_div_we) send_dummy <= 1;` which starts a 15-cycle `send_bitcnt` idle dummy on divider write, holding `send_bitcnt!=0` so the following `reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt` data load is blocked and `ser_tx` stays at `send_pattern[0]=1`.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -109,6 +109,6 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		if (reg_div_we)
-			send_dummy <= 1;
+			send_dummy <= 0;
 		send_divcnt <= send_divcnt + 1;
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			send_pattern <= ~1;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5 matched, checksum != 9e1b73c13d0a095f6b9512137fc937a720f9b8a80231ffc4b660d6d1459f6985"}

